Z||000000||85seNUT||01-24-2001||02:18 AM||||After you swap the 3.4 into your car, can u still buy parts for it that are made for fieros?  like if i was to buy the hypertech chip would it be usefull on my car since its not the standard 2.8.  ||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfiero||01-24-2001||02:53 AM||||Yes.  It will still be a Fiero, just more displacement.  This is the advantage of this swap......since you will be using the stock Fiero intake, stock wiring stock ECM, etc. you can continue to purchase parts as if it were a stock Fiero.  Almost all parts are interchangeable bewteen the 2.8, 3.1 &  3.4.<P><BR>A guy named Joe Wynman sells a custom burned PROM chip for a 3.4 w/manual tranny.  I don't have his e-mail address handy, but I will post it as soon as I dig it up.  It's my understanding that his chip will give you better gains than the aftermarket ones, as it is customized for the Fiero with a transplanted 3.4.         ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Alex4mula||01-24-2001||08:46 AM||||Hey mrfiero (or any other); Could you give more info on this Joe Wynman guy? I would be interested in that chip for my 3.4 Formula. Tks.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Black88GT||01-24-2001||09:25 AM||||fierojo@bellatlantic.net<P>For 19# injectors and 5 speed manual 3.4<P>Cost is 100 plus 5 dollars shipping.<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||MooCow||01-24-2001||02:01 PM||||You can reach him between 6 and 9 pm EST, at 201-457-9507.  Does anyone here have this chip?  According to Ed Parks it is a great upgrade to do to your 3.4 conversion.<P>                               Thanks Ken||||reg||1
Z||000005||mshill||01-24-2001||02:30 PM||||In doing my swap I have only found a couple of parts that are different between the stock 2.8L and the 3.4L:<P>1) Pistons, rings, head gaskets (bigger bore)<BR>2) Rods (bigger stroke)<BR>3) Timing chain guide. (no alignment guide on one hole like 2.8)<P>If I think of any more I will update the thread.||||reg||1
