Z||000012||87ECO5||02-19-2001||09:41 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by mrfiero:<BR><B>A guy named Joe Wynman sells a custom burned PROM chip for a 3.4 w/manual tranny.  I don't have his e-mail address handy, but I will post it as soon as I dig it up.  It's my understanding that his chip will give you better gains than the aftermarket ones, as it is customized for the Fiero with a transplanted 3.4.         </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>What kind of gains are we talking about?||||reg||1
Z||000013||Black88GT||02-19-2001||01:35 PM||||I am hoping to call Joe tonight to get more info.  But, from what I understand, it eliminates the EGR and helps the computer deal with the air/fuel mix, because many 3.4 owners have noticed the car runs too rich.<P>I will update this hopefully tonight after I talked to him...<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000014||MooCow||02-19-2001||03:47 PM||||Yes please let em know what the gains are on this chip.  I would like to know if I should look into buying one or not real soon.<P>                              Thanks Ken<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/kensig_1.jpg"> ||||reg||10
Z||000015||fierosound||02-19-2001||05:43 PM||||I just installed the PROM from J. Wynman.  I noticed the engine idled and ran smoother right away.  At WOT I didn't notice that much difference over the Hypertech Stage II I was running.  I still have some tuning to do such as bump up the fuel pressure and advance the timing as recommended by Wynman, so that may better my performace at WOT.<P>He also recommends oversize fuel injectors with this chip.  Summit part# FMS-M9593A302 or Ford Motorsports M-9593-A302.  These are rated at 24lb/hr.  Stock 3.4L injectors will run lean and damage the engine.<P>Documentation with the PROM:<P>1- The built-in engine RPM limiter has its top end cut-out point increased to 6700RPM, and it's cut-in set to 5000RPM.  The cut-out point is the engine speed where the ECM turns off the fuel injectors in order to protec the engine. The cut-in point is where the fuel injectors are re-energized and normal engine operation resumes..<P>2-ALDL data stream changes - PROM ID is SW version ID, O2 sensor cross count is current air/fuel ratio (AFR), 126=12.6/1 AFR.  This information is only available with a scan tool via the ALDL connector.<P>3-Coolant temperture points are changed for operation with 180-degree thermostat which is included in the Deluxe PROM kit.  This is the temperature where the ECM enters its "learn mode" and is considered to be in closed loop mode.<P>4-Fuel de-accelation cut-off is disabled, no more annoying bump as the engine RPMs crosses below 1600 RPM.  The stock PROM "turns off" the fuel injectors during coast down conditions.  When the accelerator pedal is then depressed, there is a slight delay in re-energizing the fuel injectors.  This wass felt by the driver as a slight hesitation.<P>5.EGR operation disabled, no need to mechanically disable EGR valve.  The fuel and spark tables have been adjusted for this type of operation.  Please note; this change violates the emmission certification of your Fiero.<P>6. The Wide-Open Throttle (WOT) fuel ratio has been enriched.<P>7. Spark advance curves custom fitted to 3.4L engine.<P>There's additional information on installing the chip, setting timing etc.<P><p>[This message has been edited by fierosound (edited 02-20-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000016||Alex4mula||02-19-2001||08:53 PM||||3.4L injectors will run lean and damage the engine??? Pardon me but I don't buy that. Currently I'm running 2.8 injectors in my 3.4 & my AutoXRay doesn't show a lean condiion. 24# injectors seems a little big to me for a stock or mildly modified 3.4. If you run nitrous or turbo then ok. I'm running a Hypertech stage III chip which disables EGR & use low temp stat also. I wonder what will be different in this one.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000017||fierosound||02-20-2001||01:39 AM||||Alex...<P>In his documentation, the oversize injectors are his recommendation, and that's what his fuel tables are set for.  Probably not enough difference between this and the Hypertech Stage III for you to bother getting it.  For more information, send an email to J. Wynman.  He may be able to explain it more.||||reg||10
Z||000018||THE BEAST||02-20-2001||05:40 PM||||"5.EGR operation disabled, no need to mechanically disable EGR valve. The fuel and spark tables have been adjusted for this type of operation. Please note; this change violates the emmission certification of your Fiero."<P>I thought that if you disabled the EGR valve you would make the car run so lean that it would burn one of you piston or two (I can't remember which one). Sorry but I don't understand. Could you explain it to me, please. Thank you - The BEAST.||||reg||5
Z||000019||fierosound||02-20-2001||07:25 PM||||Beast...<P>That is probably the reason Wynman is recommending the oversize injectors.  This chip is highly recommended by Ed Parks who's done numerous 3.4L swaps.  I'm sure Wynman knows what he's talking about.  I'm no expert by any means, but more elaborate answers would come from Wynman and should be emailed to Wynman.  Email address is in a message above...||||reg||10
Z||000020||Tom Philips||02-21-2001||07:53 AM||||By diabling egr with stock prom you will notice that you will get more detonation(spark knock) because egr acts as a dilutant and the engine is more spark tolerant... so by disconnecting egr the engine will not run lean because the o2 sensor will still adjust to a stoich mixture of 14.6:1 A/F mixture.... this is why when some aftermarket prom manufacturers change the spark table with no egr it is to keep the engine out of spark knock||||reg||1
Z||000021||fierosound||02-22-2001||10:56 PM||||Joe Wynman's got a nice North-south LT1 conversion<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Wyman_1.jpg">  <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000022||mshill||02-23-2001||04:24 PM||||Shweeeeeet!!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Wonder what transaxle he used on that.||||reg||1
